	<h2>Who we are</h2>
	<p>
		An eight-pillar Asian modern-luxury publication — Style, Beauty, Dining, Travel,
		Living, People, Culture and Guides — built on rigorous editorial standards and
		a documented editorial process. Paid work is held to the same accuracy, sourcing and
		image-rights standards as independent editorial.
	</p>

	<h2>Why partner with us</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>An editorially defined audience.</strong> Readers interested in Asian style, tropical beauty and considered dining and travel.</li>
		<li><strong>Editorial integration.</strong> Sponsored features written in the same pillar voice as our reported work — clearly labelled, never banner copy.</li>
		<li><strong>Measured proposals.</strong> We share only analytics we can verify, with the reporting period and method attached.</li>
		<li><strong>Flexible formats.</strong> Pillar features, founder profiles, Arahkaii Weekly sponsorship and bespoke partnerships.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What we never run</h2>
	<p>
		We do not publish alcohol, bar, nightclub, wine, beer, cocktail or nightlife
		advertising in any form. This is a permanent editorial position, not a negotiable —
		and a large part of why our readers trust what they find here.
	</p>

	<h2>Opportunities</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Sponsored articles &amp; brand features</li>
		<li>Newsletter sponsorship</li>
		<li>Social &amp; creator campaigns</li>
		<li>Event partnerships &amp; launch amplification</li>
		<li>Clearly bounded pillar partnerships</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Labelling and brand safety</h2>
	<p>
		Paid work begins with a visible “Paid partnership” disclosure naming the partner.
		Affiliate relationships and supplied access are disclosed separately. Partners may check
		factual brand details, but Arahkaii retains final control of the headline, conclusions and publication.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>
	<p>
		For current formats, founding-partner rates and a tailored proposal, write to
		<a href="mailto:hello@arahkaii.com">hello@arahkaii.com</a>. Tell us about your brand
		and what you'd like the reader to remember. A dated, metrics-backed media kit will be
		published after the site has a sufficient continuous analytics history; we do not publish estimated reach as fact.
	</p>
